2026-11-18T20:42:29.6130148Z    image gate: reid_house_2013_prairie inland_architect_plate: verdict "differs", 4 difference(s) open: the two oval lights in the upper wall, at the frame's two sides about 7.3 m up (x 340-370 and 575-600 px); the frame round the three-light storeys: pilasters at 1.85 and 5.27 m from the second floor's belt to the frieze, sunk panels between the two floors' lights and a corniced hood over each storey's lights; the entablature's frieze of garlands and wreaths and the dentils under the cornice's corona (x 300-615 px, y 160-335); the front's tone: the plate prints it the palest front on the block, near white beside 2011's pale stone, where the render's cream brick reads a warm tan
